Butter-Braised Slow Cooker Chicken

Tender, fall-apart chicken thighs slow-cooked in rich butter and salt. A pure, high-fat carnivore staple with zero carbs.

---

* **Difficulty:** Easy
* **Prep Time:** 5 minutes
* **Cook Time:** 4 hours (High) or 7 hours (Low)
* **Servings:** 4

### Nutrition Info (Per Serving)

| Calories | Protein | Fat | Carbs |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 540 | 38g | 42g | 0g |

---

### Ingredients

* **2 lbs** Chicken Thighs (bone-in, skin-on for maximum fat)
* **1/2 cup** Grass-fed Butter (salted)
* **1 tbsp** Coarse Sea Salt (or Redmond Real Salt)
* **Optional:** 1/4 cup bone broth (if your slow cooker runs very hot)

---

### Instructions

1. **Prep the Chicken:** Pat the chicken thighs dry with a paper towel. This helps the fat render more cleanly.
2. **Season:** Generously coat all sides of the chicken with the sea salt.
3. **Layer:** Place the chicken thighs into the slow cooker. Cut the butter into small pats and distribute them evenly over the top of the meat.
4. **Cook:** Cover and cook on **Low for 6–7 hours** or **High for 3–4 hours**. The chicken should be "fork-tender" and pulling away from the bone.
5. **Finish:** Once finished, shred the meat directly in the pot, allowing it to soak up the rendered chicken fat and melted butter.
6. **Serve:** Serve in a bowl, ensuring you pour the remaining "liquid gold" (butter and fat) from the pot over the meat.

---

> **Pro Tip:** If you prefer crispy skin, you can sear the thighs in a hot cast-iron pan for 2 minutes per side before placing them in the slow cooker.
